ood its distinctive flavor, which can affect the quality of clinical nutrition products.", "PRODUCTO:The PRODUCTO refers to the clinical nutrition items being developed, which are designed to maintain both organoleptic and nutritional quality. This product represents the final output of a comprehensive design and development process in clinical nutrition, undergoing various stages of testing and validation prior to its market launch.", "ALMACENAMIENTO:Storage refers to the conditions under which clinical nutrition products are kept, which can affect their quality and nutrient stability over time.", "SENSACIÓN TRIGEMINAL:Trigeminal sensation refers to the mouthfeel experienced when consuming clinical nutrition products, which can be affected by protein coagulation and viscosity.", "TRATAMIENTO TÉRMICO:", "ICIDCA:ICIDCA is an organization involved in the scientific and industrial development of products, particularly in the context of scaling processes from laboratory to industrial production.", "PHOSPHATE STABILITY TEST:The phosphate stability test involves subjecting a product to an acidic environment and heat to determine its stability and coagulation properties.", "MICROBIOLOGICAL CONTROLS:Microbiological controls are evaluations conducted to confirm the effectiveness of thermal treatment in ensuring product sterility and safety.", "PHYSICAL-CHEMICAL CONTROLS:Physical-chemical controls are measures taken during product development to assess various attributes such as pH, viscosity, and particle size distribution.", "SENSORY EVALUATION:Sensory evaluation involves internal tastings to assess and select samples based on their organoleptic properties like color, odor, flavor, and texture.", "LABORATORY SCALE:Laboratory scale refers to the initial phase of product development where experiments are conducted to achieve desired results before scaling up."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty"